out at /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies alone, because it holds uncommitted BIM work. Work only in your worktree. Absolute paths into that checkout are fine for reading `Equipment Room.ply`, and nothing else there should be read as current code.\n\nSteps:\n1. In your worktree, create branch `viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects` from origin/main (5179efa).\n2. Before writing anything, look at `origin/eduard` (web/route.js, web/main.js, web/objects.js, app/api/main.py, app/api/store.py, app/nav/). Routing is Eduard's area and that unmerged branch changes this code. If it already fixes the bug, stop and report that instead of duplicating it.\n3. Trace the path with `entire graph` and then the source: the live preview during a drag, what is saved on drop, and every later re-plan (camera moves, Walk following, starting a walk, reload). Find out why a re-plan loses the chair's new position. Consider the viewer's request, the backend's footprints, any fallback that drops footprints when no route is found or when the start lies inside an inflated footprint, and stale state.\n4. Reproduce before fixing, with the real data in the scratchpad's make_test folder and the headless browser setup you already know. Find which object is the black chair from the assets and the pre-cut pieces. Pick a target so that the chair can be dropped across the straight route. Drag it there, confirm the route bends, then move the viewer and separately walk along the route, in both Walk and Fly. After every re-plan, check `route.state.route.path` against the chair's current footprint plus clearance. Record the failing numbers.\n5. Fix the root cause with the smallest complete change. Add a regression test in `tests/` if any of the cause is in Python. For a viewer-only cause, keep the browser script in the scratchpad and report its output.\n6. Verify: the reproduction now passes; the chair's old spot is walkable again; undo restores the original route; a reload keeps the moved chair blocking; `make lint` and the full pytest command from your notes both pass.\n7. Commit on your branch with the required Co-Authored-By trailer, including an updated `handoffs/viktortrilar.md` for this branch. Add to `docs/USAGE.md` only if what it says becomes wrong. Do not push, do not open a PR, and do not merge.\n\nPractical limits: the main session is using ports 8001, 8123 and 8124, so use other ports such as 8201 and 8223, and only kill processes you started, by PID or on your own ports. If the proxy in `web/serve.py` is fixed to 8001, work around it for testing without committing that workaround. Put scratch files in a new `route_fix` folder inside the scratchpad and treat `make_test` as read-only.\n\nReport back with: the root cause with file:line references; what you changed; what you ran and the before and after numbers; the branch name and worktree path; whether it will conflict with `origin/eduard`; and anything you could not verify.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/tasks/aef4b903dc16194fa.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"caaa3635-9f13-4e86-9841-14f130262158","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","branch":"viktor/bim","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":7,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":3},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0be47d92-b2d6-428c-9f96-b9e0604bcfca","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","sou