udes operator changes\n**Blockers:** an agent is fixing routes that ignore moved objects on `viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects`, not finished. Roihu closed until at least Monday. Local branch viktor/viewer-objects holds an unused merge: don't merge it\n\"\"\")\nEOF\ngit add app/extract/primitives.py tests/test_primitives.py Makefile docs/RESULTS.md && git commit -q -m \"Don't trust cylinders fitted to nearly flat arcs\n\nA nearly flat surface fits any large circle, so obj-0144 became a tank 2.08 m\nacross on a 1 m wide object, reaching 1.26 m through the wall. It keeps its box\nnow. make shapes applies the rule to the Release's copy, and make bim runs it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git add web/bim.js docs/USAGE.md handoffs/viktortrilar.md && git commit -q -m \"Show objects made in the viewer in BIM mode\n\nA split hid the original while its parts had no element, so both disappeared\nfrom the model. They show as plain boxes now. The usage guide also said make bim\npicks up operator changes, which it can't, as they stay in the backend.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git log --format='%h %an %s' -4 | cut -c1-90; git status --short | cut -c1-60; git fetch origin 2>&1 | tail -2 | cut -c1-90; echo \"main ahead by: $(git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/main)\"; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/bim-model-fixes 2>&1 | grep -v \"^remote:\" | tail -3 | cut -c1-120; cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad/pr1.md <<'EOF'\nAdds Sasha's BIM mode from `yasasha/bim` (commit c478873, unchanged) with fixes for what checking it found.\n\n**From Sasha:** a BIM button that swaps the scan for a 3D model of 445 elements, with class filters, IFC properties, isolate and a height cut, plus `make bim` for an IFC4 file with no new package.\n\n**Fixes on top:**\n- **Oversized tank:** `obj-0144` was fitted 2.08 m across on a 1 m wide object and reached 1.26 m through the wall. Cylinders from nearly flat arcs now count as poor fits, so it keeps its box. Only this object changes: the other 64 fits are the same.\n- **Release data:** the Release's `shapes.json` still has the bad fit, so `make shapes` fits again locally, and `make bim` runs it. This needs `Equipment Room.ply` and takes seconds on a CPU.\n- **Split objects vanished from BIM mode:** the original was hidden while its parts had no element. Objects added, split or combined in the viewer now show as plain see-through boxes, marked unconfirmed.\n- **Usage guide:** it said re-running `make bim` picks up operator changes. It can't, because they stay in the backend. The guide now says what the IFC leaves out.\n\n**Tested:**\n- 223 tests passed, 2 skipped, lint clean. The IFC checks ran locally, because CI doesn't have IfcOpenShell.\n- Real scene: 0 IFC schema issues, 445 elements.\n- Headless browser, main plus these changes: entering BIM mode, route to P-005, moving the cart (route 4.35 m to 5.5 m, box follows), tapping objects, height cut, split parts showing and undo removing them, no page errors.\n\n**Not tested:** opening the IFC in a real BIM tool, the 5090, a tablet.\n\n**After pulling:** run `make bim`, then restart the viewer.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ngh pr create --base main --head viktor/bim-model-fixes --title \"Add Sasha's BIM mode, with fixes for an oversized tank and split objects\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad/pr1.md 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-100","description":"Commit the fixes, push the branch and open the pull request","timeout":120000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"81d414b3-702b-4ad6-881e-7cf832c1dd88","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgobLV4U33Kiqr3sM4SuW","requestRef":"953271a1-26b2-4847-9566-61054358d8f5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb806